            <ArticleTitle>The First Case Report of a Systemic Allergy to OnabotulinumtoxinA (Botox) in a Healthy Patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>766-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/1090820X14532648</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="UNLABELLED">To the authors' knowledge, this is the first report of an allergy to onabotulinumtoxinA. The 43-year-old woman experienced severe itching after injection of Botox and Juvéderm. Results of prick and patch testing confirmed a T-cell-mediated allergy to Botox. This case can aid in the evaluation of suspected allergies to Botox.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="LEVEL OF EVIDENCE" NlmCategory="METHODS">5.</AbstractText>
